Z||000004||stsmithgt||03-16-2001||01:11 PM||||I tend to look for quality, service and convenience like most people. I will pay more to avoid bad service or quality within reason.  That's why I appreciated the conduct of the Fiero Store.  I enjoyed seeing my parts on the porch when I got home yesterday.<P>It reminds me of the saying,<BR>"PRICE,SERVICE,QUALITY....PICK TWO!"  This defines many shops.  Except a couple I know of here in the Monterey area, W****** G*****.  They did fix my A/C after 4 return visits for about $1400.บบ.Not convenient and high priced.  Can you say,"Bend over!" I did go back for them to fix an exhaust leak from the front manifold.  Big mistake.  5 visits later, it was way too high a price, POOR quality workmanship and very inconvenient.  I'm not pointing a finger at the establishment entirely.  The mechanic must have been deaf and unhappy with his job from what I saw of his work on my exhaust.  Finally S***** A*** and E******* The ol' pick-up coil went out on my car.  I didn't know, I only had my car a few months and this was it's first break down.  Four days later, they had it fixed with the addition of cutting up a harness for nothing.  They tried to convince me the surface rust on the coils ferrite was what made it all fail.  For $650.บบ   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif"> I got my car back.  The rare of all rare, the tire store I go to has a good price, great service with quality to boot.  The Monterey Tire Center.  Thanks Paul. (My brother takes care of the Manager's Motorcycle)   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR>   I guess my point is right out of that "saying".  You have to have of those qualities, though effort does score brownie points,  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> or I'll eventually stop going back the next time I have a problem.  This is only common sense right?  <BR>Anyway, have to go back to work. LATER!<p>[This message has been edited by stsmithgt (edited 03-16-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000005||My7Fieros||03-16-2001||02:49 PM||||<B>DUDE!!!!! 65O BUCKS FOR A PICK UP COIL!!!</B> They cost $8.50 at autozone and take about 20 to 30 minutes to install (depending on how stubborn your alt. is comming out).<BR>Ive replaced them on every one of my Fieros..one of the first things I do. Jeez, I hope they at least used a condom!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><BR>Next time, post your problem on here first!M7F||||reg||11
Z||000006||stsmithgt||03-16-2001||04:56 PM||||They said the charges were for all the time and labor they put in to diagnose, test and repair it.  I think it's more like, "We didn't know what was wrong so we used the shotgun technique to fix it by HACKING our way through your harness and replacing any related part and charged you up the shorts to cover our alcohol problem from being so incompetent at what we do." <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif"> <BR>I'm sure they laughed all the way to the bank.  I hate having only one car.  At the time I was working at least 50 hours a week and didn't have time to mess with it and <B>Wayside Garage</B> recomended them for being electronic specialists.  The more I learned about Fiero's the more I spread the word about them and the more I wanted to do certain things that weren't exactly legal.  Life's too short though.  It's not worth it. Did I say Susie's Auto and Electric? or was I not supposed to say they were in Monterey?  They can't get me for slander because I have the receipts to prove it. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> ||||reg||13
Z||000007||KRMFiero||03-16-2001||05:02 PM||||I have been ordering lots of parts from them latly, they all come in with in 1-2 days from when they were shipped (usally shipped next or same day)<P>Kyle||||reg||1
Z||000008||stsmithgt||03-16-2001||05:10 PM||||I almost forgot.  They had my car 4 days before they had it running.  They wanted to keep my car another two weeks to make sure it was fixed. WTF?  I Learned enough while my car was in the shop to know I was being bent over.  I saw what they finaly fixed so I told them I want my car back.  They told me they wouldn't back their work unless I left it there for another couple weeks for further .anal.ysis. "WARRENTY VOID" as I drove out of there <B>never</B> to return....not that it was their fault, but the pick-up coil lasted 10 months then burnt out again.<BR>and NO I didn't pay that much again OR go back. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> I was born at night, but not last night.||||reg||1
